WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:05.645
I held my breath as Holmes pulled back the curtain and revealed—four suits!

2
00:00:05.646 --> 00:00:08.933
"Oh!" Soames grabbed my arm in relief.

3
00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:12.673
I gave him a reassuring smile. "Nobody's there!"

4
00:00:12.674 --> 00:00:17.687
Meanwhile Holmes' attention was suddenly drawn to something on the floor. "What's this?"

5
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:22.311
The detective picked up a piece of black clay exactly like the one on Soames' desk.

6
00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:26.871
"Your visitor seems to have left traces in your bedroom as well as your sitting room."

7
00:00:26.872 --> 00:00:30.405
Soames looked puzzled. "What could he have wanted in here?"

8
00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:34.935
"When you came back unexpectedly, he gathered up his things and rushed into your bedroom to hide."

9
00:00:34.936 --> 00:00:37.655
Soames' eyes widened in surprise.

10
00:00:37.656 --> 00:00:42.034
"Do you mean that the whole time I was talking to Bannister, the culprit was in here?"

11
00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:45.880
"You had him prisoner, and you didn't even know it."

12
00:00:45.881 --> 00:00:48.964
Holmes rubbed his hands together and strode out of the bedroom.

13
00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:52.766
"Now, Mr. Soames, if you would be so good as to summon your servant . . ."

14
00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:58.406
*** Bannister was a short fellow in his fifties, who kept taking deep breaths to calm

15
00:00:58.407 --> 00:01:02.793
himself. I wondered if he was still suffering from the shocking disruption of his quiet routine.

16
00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:07.513
"Mr. Holmes and Dr. Watson are investigating our unhappy discovery," Soames said.

17
00:01:07.514 --> 00:01:11.772
Bannister nodded in our direction but didn't venture very far into the sitting room.

18
00:01:11.773 --> 00:01:14.781
"I understand that you left your key in the door," Holmes said.

19
00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:17.726
"Yes, sir. I had the tea tray in my hands.

20
00:01:17.727 --> 00:01:21.459
I intended to come back for the key, but then I forgot."

21
00:01:22.311 --> 00:01:26.977
"You were quite upset when you and Mr. Soames discovered that the proofs had been tampered with?"

22
00:01:26.978 --> 00:01:32.831
"Oh yes, sir. Nothing like this has ever happened since I've worked here. I nearly fainted, sir!"

23
00:01:32.832 --> 00:01:34.473
Holmes went on with his questioning.

24
00:01:34.474 --> 00:01:37.124
"And where were you when you started feeling ill?"

25
00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:38.731
"Here, near the door."

26
00:01:38.732 --> 00:01:41.837
"That's odd because you collapsed into the desk chair.

27
00:01:41.838 --> 00:01:45.579
Why did you cross the room to the desk chair when another one was right here?"

28
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.689
"I don't know, sir." Bannister nervously licked his lips.

29
00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:51.448
"I just needed to sit down."

30
00:01:51.449 --> 00:01:54.245
Soames was quick to come to Bannister's rescue.

31
00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.580
"He really was looking ghastly."

32
00:01:56.581 --> 00:01:59.250
Holmes quizzed the servant for a few more minutes.

33
00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:03.171
"What did you do after Mr. Soames went in search of me?"

34
00:02:03.172 --> 00:02:06.958
"I sat here for a few minutes, and then I locked the door and went to my room."

35
00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:11.296
"Is there anyone you think might try to cheat on the exam?" Holmes said.

36
00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.663
Bannister shook his head vehemently.

37
00:02:13.664 --> 00:02:17.731
"I can't believe that any young gentleman in this college would try such a thing!"

38
00:02:17.732 --> 00:02:20.315
"One last question," Holmes said.

39
00:02:20.316 --> 00:02:24.480
"Have you mentioned this incident to the three students who live above Mr. Soames?"

40
00:02:24.481 --> 00:02:27.599
Bannister said no, and Holmes dismissed him.

41
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.419
"Now, Mr. Soames, let's return to the courtyard."

42
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.466
Holmes headed outside, but I remained with Soames while he locked his door.

43
00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:38.966
When we reached the courtyard, Holmes was looking up at the rooms above Soames' rooms.

44
00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:43.116
It was dark outside now, and lights were on in all three rooms.

45
00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:49.805
"Your three birds are in their nests," Holmes said, "but one of them seems restless."

46
00:02:49.806 --> 00:02:53.160
Daulat Ras' silhouette appeared on his shade, pacing.

47
00:02:53.161 --> 00:02:58.616
"I'd like to talk to each of them without giving away my purpose," Holmes said. "Is that possible?"

48
00:02:58.617 --> 00:03:02.928
"Yes, it should be easy." Soames turned to lead us inside.

49
00:03:02.929 --> 00:03:05.512
"These rooms are some of the oldest in the college.

50
00:03:05.513 --> 00:03:08.143
It's not unusual for visitors to want to see them." Soames

51
00:03:08.144 --> 00:03:12.215
was about to knock on Richard Gilchrist's door when Holmes cautioned him. "No

52
00:03:12.216 --> 00:03:15.865
names, please. I don't want anyone to know who I am." After

53
00:03:15.866 --> 00:03:19.238
Soames knocked, a tall, blond student let us in. The

54
00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:25.542
room did contain some interesting architectural details, and Holmes was particularly delighted by the fireplace. He

55
00:03:26.152 --> 00:03:30.218
was in the midst of sketching it in his notebook when his pencil broke. After

56
00:03:30.219 --> 00:03:36.164
borrowing a pencil from Gilchrist, he resumed sketching and then borrowed a knife to sharpen his own pencil. The

57
00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:38.555
same thing happened in Ras' room. The

58
00:03:38.556 --> 00:03:43.011
student eyed us skeptically but produced a pencil and a knife for Holmes to use. Miles

59
00:03:43.012 --> 00:03:46.460
McLaren was the only student who refused to let us in. "I

60
00:03:46.461 --> 00:03:49.961
don't care who you are!" he shouted through his closed door. "Go

61
00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:53.032
away! I'm studying for an important exam." "What

62
00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:57.581
a rude fellow!" Soames huffed and led us back downstairs. "Of

63
00:03:57.582 --> 00:04:02.560
course, he didn't realize I was at the door too, but his behavior was disrespectful and suspicious." I

64
00:04:02.561 --> 00:04:05.971
found Holmes' next question to be rather strange. He

65
00:04:06.483 --> 00:04:09.357
asked Soames how tall McLaren was. "Really,

66
00:04:09.358 --> 00:04:14.024
Mr. Holmes, I have no idea." Soames seemed impatient and annoyed. "I

67
00:04:14.025 --> 00:04:17.052
would say he's taller than Ras but shorter than Gilchrist." "That

68
00:04:17.053 --> 00:04:21.051
could be important," Holmes said. "And now I wish you good night." "What?"

69
00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:23.895
Soames uttered a cry of dismay. "Surely

70
00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.456
you're not going to leave me now! You

71
00:04:26.457 --> 00:04:28.961
don't seem to understand the position I'm in. If

72
00:04:28.962 --> 00:04:33.214
you don't find the culprit soon, I can't allow the exam to take place tomorrow." Holmes

73
00:04:33.215 --> 00:04:37.434
tried to soothe him. "There's no need to take any action tonight. Finish

74
00:04:37.435 --> 00:04:40.301
reading your proofs and send them to the printer. When

75
00:04:40.302 --> 00:04:44.749
I return first thing tomorrow, I hope to be able to straighten everything out." "

76
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.749
Hope ?" Soames

77
00:04:48.465 --> 00:04:52.178
cried. From the look on his face, Soames was obviously not

78
00:04:52.179 --> 00:04:58.754
soothed. But Holmes left the teacher's rooms anyway, taking the two pieces of black clay, the pencil shavings, and the broken

79
00:04:58.755 --> 00:05:02.604
lead. As we went through the college gates, Holmes asked my opinion on the

80
00:05:02.605 --> 00:05:07.997
case. "I'd say McLaren is guilty because he wouldn't let us in, but Ras was acting suspiciously

81
00:05:07.998 --> 00:05:11.615
too. Why was he pacing across his room if he wasn't anxious about something?"

82
00:05:11.616 --> 00:05:15.144
"Many people do that when they're trying to memorize something," Holmes said.

83
00:05:15.145 --> 00:05:17.670
"Yes, but he looked annoyed when we met him."

84
00:05:17.671 --> 00:05:22.540
"You'd look annoyed too, Watson, if two strangers invaded your room while you were preparing for an important exam.

85
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:24.459
No, I don't have a problem with that.

86
00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.826
And there was nothing strange about the students' pencils and knives.

87
00:05:28.811 --> 00:05:32.104
"But Bannister puzzles me. What's he up to?"

88
00:05:32.105 --> 00:05:34.755
"He seemed honest to me," I said.

89
00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:37.547
"Exactly," Holmes said as we crossed the street.

90
00:05:37.548 --> 00:05:40.498
"So, why would an honest man—oh, never mind.

91
00:05:40.499 --> 00:05:45.345
Let's go into this stationery store. Luckily, the shops stay open late in this college town."

92
00:05:45.346 --> 00:05:50.126
At each of our four stationery stores, Holmes showed his pencil shavings to a clerk.

93
00:05:50.127 --> 00:05:55.543
The clerks all recognized the Faber brand, but none remembered selling the unusual blue pencil.

94
00:05:55.544 --> 00:06:01.662
Back on the street, Holmes sighed. "That wasn't very helpful, but I think I know who the cheater is."

95
00:06:01.663 --> 00:06:06.861
"Who?" At this point I was desperately hungry for supper and wanted a break from this case.

96
00:06:06.862 --> 00:06:10.094
"Patience, my dear Watson." Holmes smiled at me.

97
00:06:10.095 --> 00:06:14.923
"All will be revealed tomorrow—after I check one final detail."

